WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.063
- You got married!

00:00:01.063 --> 00:00:02.722
I've been noticing that rock, Miss Thing.

00:00:02.722 --> 00:00:03.555
(laughing)

00:00:03.555 --> 00:00:04.388
You got married this Spring, right?

00:00:04.388 --> 00:00:06.010
- I did, I got married in March.

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:08.004
- Yay! Are you still
in the honeymoon phase?

00:00:08.004 --> 00:00:10.180
- You know, yeah, definitely.

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:13.660
I feel like we got
married and then went on

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:14.640
an awesome honeymoon,

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.690
and then I just jumped right into work.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.450
So, I would definitely advise
any like, brides to be like,

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.520
give yourself like, a little
bit more time to like,

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:22.700
but it is still so nice.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.936
I say husband so much it's obnoxious.

00:00:24.936 --> 00:00:25.840
Like, literally.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.080
- Oh, when we got married, my
husband and I, we literally,

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.170
we're so dorky, I was
so excited because I was

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:32.003
never married before and I was like,

00:00:32.003 --> 00:00:33.436
"I'm changing your name
to husband in my phone."

00:00:33.436 --> 00:00:34.269
- I did too!

00:00:34.269 --> 00:00:35.102
(laughing and applause)

00:00:35.102 --> 00:00:35.935
- I did!

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:38.640
- Except it's a "Husband" and
then I put a red heart emoji--

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:39.473
- Oh, I'm not as cute as you.

00:00:39.473 --> 00:00:40.306
- So then when he calls it's like,

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:43.500
"Husband, red heart, husband, red heart."

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.460
- It says that?

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.293
- Yeah.

00:00:45.293 --> 00:00:46.126
- That's amazing!

00:00:46.126 --> 00:00:46.959
- Yeah.

00:00:46.959 --> 00:00:47.810
- Let's talk about music,

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:50.020
what are like, your
songs that inspire you?

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:50.940
- Oh my Gosh!

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.580
- Because you sing so many genres,

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.000
I do that as well, so I was just curious.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.388
- But you know how hard that is, like,

00:00:56.388 --> 00:01:00.162
I would say the first
song for me would be this

00:01:00.162 --> 00:01:03.790
Castle on a Cloud which is
the song I sang in Les Mis.

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:06.400
Because I'd never sang before in my life,

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.910
and then I went for an
open call for Les Mis

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.860
in my hometown, sang that
song, and got the part

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.428
and was on Broadway two weeks later.

00:01:13.428 --> 00:01:16.950
(applause and cheering)

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:17.800
- Hashtag blessed.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:18.890
- It was kinda crazy.

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:19.723
- That's awesome!

00:01:19.723 --> 00:01:20.556
- And then I've been working.

00:01:20.556 --> 00:01:23.520
So, that song, I also love
anything on Jagged Little Pill,

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.230
that was the first record I ever bought.

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:26.941
- Yes, perfect! I love that song.

00:01:26.941 --> 00:01:28.782
- And then, Don't Rain
on my Parade because--

00:01:28.782 --> 00:01:29.615
- That's one of my favorites.

00:01:29.615 --> 00:01:30.448
- Oh, really?

00:01:30.448 --> 00:01:31.281
- I love Funny Girl.

00:01:31.281 --> 00:01:32.114
- Oh, me too.

00:01:32.114 --> 00:01:34.082
- It was my like, first movie musical.

00:01:34.082 --> 00:01:34.915
- Get in line, Kelly, get in line!

00:01:34.915 --> 00:01:37.040
- Yeah, I love it, I love Barbara, I do.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:39.100
- And then, don't think
I'm like, just saying this,

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.375
but Since You've Been
Gone for me was like--

00:01:40.375 --> 00:01:41.997
- Oh you're such a--

00:01:41.997 --> 00:01:44.648
- I'm serious. Wait, well, what are yours?

00:01:44.648 --> 00:01:49.064
- Mine, Why, Annie Lennox is
definitely one of my favorites.

00:01:49.064 --> 00:01:50.290
- You have a lot of Annie Lennox stuff,

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:53.700
And then she gives a cute
little gift bag to everyone.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.524
- A wine and vinyl.
It's my favorite thing.

00:01:55.524 --> 00:01:56.357
- I love that.

00:01:56.357 --> 00:01:58.392
- Yes, I love wine and
vinyl at the same time.

00:01:58.392 --> 00:01:59.260
- Okay, Annie Lennox.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:00.420
- So, Why, Annie Lennox.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:04.743
I'd probably say Bonnie
Raitt, Love Me Like a Man.

00:02:04.743 --> 00:02:05.576
Woo!

00:02:05.576 --> 00:02:07.160
And I'm talking about the live version,

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.268
the record version's all right,

00:02:08.268 --> 00:02:10.133
the live version is a jam.

00:02:11.206 --> 00:02:15.070
And then I'd say I've Never
Loved a Man, by Aretha Franklin.

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:15.903
- Oh yeah.

00:02:17.061 --> 00:02:20.047
- But, I feel like I also do like men.

00:02:20.047 --> 00:02:21.070
(laughter)

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:23.017
I don't know why I picked just women.

00:02:23.017 --> 00:02:24.330
- Well, I picked all girls.
I love female singers.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.756
- Well, we're female
singers, so that's why.

00:02:25.756 --> 00:02:26.589
- But I do, I really do.

00:02:26.589 --> 00:02:27.422
Everyone's like, "What do you listen to?

00:02:27.422 --> 00:02:28.255
"What kind of music do you like?"

00:02:28.255 --> 00:02:30.443
I'm like, "Any girls,
like any girl singers."

00:02:30.443 --> 00:02:32.690
- I don't want any girl,
I want powerful women.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:35.036
- Well yeah, but I'm into
like, it could be country--

00:02:35.036 --> 00:02:35.869
- It's sexy!

00:02:35.869 --> 00:02:38.030
it could be pop, it could
be any female vocalist,

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:39.489
I'm just like, give it to me.

00:02:39.489 --> 00:02:40.322
They're my favorite.

00:02:40.322 --> 00:02:41.155
- Yes, I'm the same.

00:02:41.155 --> 00:02:42.047
- Sorry boys.

00:02:42.047 --> 00:02:42.880
(laughter)

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:44.400
- All right, so, tell
us about your new album,

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.233
your Christmas project.

00:02:45.233 --> 00:02:47.130
- Yeah, it's my first Christmas record,

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:49.217
it's coming out, it's called
Christmas in the City.

00:02:49.217 --> 00:02:50.104
And for me--

00:02:50.104 --> 00:02:50.937
(applause and cheering)

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:51.785
- Oh yeah, there it is!

00:02:51.785 --> 00:02:52.645
- Look at that dress!

00:02:52.645 --> 00:02:57.354
- Thank you. I'm from New York,
born and raised in the city,

00:02:57.354 --> 00:02:59.206
and I moved out here 10 years ago,

00:02:59.206 --> 00:03:01.870
and the one thing I've really
missed are my Christmases

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:02.730
in New York.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:03.917
And I go home every holiday--

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:04.750
- It's beautiful.

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.610
- But it's the best,
and so this is all about

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:08.286
that time of year that
reminds me of family,

00:03:08.286 --> 00:03:09.810
and being with friends,

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:12.760
and being where I was,
you know, born and raised,

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:16.420
and I just picked all of my
favorite Christmas songs.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.553
It was just amazing.

